WEBVTT

00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:10.000
Yes! An out-of-season research project

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.917
for our assassination classroom:

00:00:12.917 --> 00:00:17.583
Hijack the space station
and steal their experiment data!

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:23.833
And so the E Class's unprecedented
research project began.

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:26.167
"The reentry capsule
carrying the research data

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.625
will splash down in the Pacific Ocean.

00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:32.583
The capsule will be transported
to the lab unopened,

00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:37.417
to prevent unlikely theft of
the same by the target supercreature."

00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:40.208
Very clever precautions indeed.

00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:43.250
I can't carry anything too heavy.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:48.000
Use a five-ton capsule as a safe
and there's no way I can steal it.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.417
That's why we get them to show
us while it's still in space.

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:55.958
But does Japan really have the tech
to launch a manned rocket?

00:00:55.958 --> 00:00:59.292
Their technology is
reliable enough for that, anyway.

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:03.792
My influence might have moved things along.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:08.542
There was plenty to fear,
of course, but more than anything,

00:01:08.542 --> 00:01:12.292
we had fun coming together
to tackle challenges--

00:01:12.292 --> 00:01:15.375
we could forget about all our uncertainties.

00:01:21.375 --> 00:01:23.792
<i>"Wait, just hang on a sec!"</i>

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:26.792
<i>I scream, but it gets me nowhere</i>

00:01:26.792 --> 00:01:29.250
<i>I put all my strength into being afraid of</i>

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.042
<i>The limits that just kept on closing in</i>

00:01:32.042 --> 00:01:34.583
<i>Reality is merciless</i>

00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:37.292
<i>And time is especially tricky</i>

00:01:37.292 --> 00:01:42.542
<i>It's like someone's snatching away</i>
<i>the blanket I just can't sleep without</i>

00:01:42.542 --> 00:01:48.625
<i>We laughed and fretted</i>

00:01:48.625 --> 00:01:53.208
<i>Over silly things, nonsensical things</i>

00:01:53.208 --> 00:01:59.333
<i>Once the final bell rings out</i>

00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:03.917
<i>The fun times will be over, too</i>

00:02:03.917 --> 00:02:05.458
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:11.458
<i>365 days' worth of lessons shoved into bags</i>

00:02:11.458 --> 00:02:14.542
<i>Like always, like it's "see you tomorrow"</i>

00:02:14.542 --> 00:02:16.083
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:16.083 --> 00:02:20.167
<i>365 days' worth of happenings</i>

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:25.167
<i>If you've made me an adult,</i>
<i>don't be showing me tears</i>

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:26.667
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.125
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:30.750
"53 Days Till Koro Sensei's Dead-Line"
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.292
<i>Even if I grow up some more</i>

00:02:33.292 --> 00:02:36.125
<i>They still won't fade a bit</i>

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.000
"19th Period: Outer Space Time"

00:02:50.917 --> 00:02:52.958
Our plans are in place.

00:02:52.958 --> 00:02:55.167
Now to put them into action.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:58.500
The rocket will only hold
two people. Who wants to go?

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.917
Me!

00:03:01.792 --> 00:03:03.042
Right?

00:03:03.042 --> 00:03:05.792
Oho, the boys, eh?

00:03:05.792 --> 00:03:09.458
It's an experimental vessel
with no successful flights yet...

00:03:09.458 --> 00:03:11.500
Who <i>still </i>wants to go?

00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:14.250
Right?

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.500
I still want to.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.042
"Tentacle"

00:03:17.042 --> 00:03:20.375
"Tentacle"
A rocket would make any mech-head's mouth water.

00:03:20.375 --> 00:03:23.292
"Tentacle"
But I'll give up my seat this time.

00:03:23.292 --> 00:03:25.125
Nagisa. Karma.

00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:30.708
Huh? I'm not big on these
risky challenges that rely on others.

00:03:30.708 --> 00:03:33.250
Just send Terasaka up with a dummy.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.167
If it crashes, no harm done.

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.333
What?!

00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:41.125
Karma the fighter, to provoke;
Nagisa the assassin, for safety.

00:03:41.125 --> 00:03:44.333
They might be a good choice
for hijacking a space station.

00:03:44.333 --> 00:03:48.125
Yeah. We'll save our money and pay our own way.

00:03:48.125 --> 00:03:53.917
"Tentacle"
You two fought hard enough to bring the whole class together!

00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:56.500
"Tentacle"
Take responsibility and lead the way!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.417
"Tentacle"
Karma?

00:03:58.417 --> 00:03:59.958
Let's give it a shot.

00:03:59.958 --> 00:04:03.500
A graduation trip to
outer space with your friend?

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.125
What could be better?

00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:06.583
"Tentacle"

00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:10.250
"Tentacle"
Okay, okay. I did promise I'd hear you out.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.083
Well! That's that!

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.750
"Cape Shimazu Space Center"

00:04:49.042 --> 00:04:50.958
Wow, cool!

00:04:50.958 --> 00:04:52.792
--This is where you launch the rockets, right?
--Hey! You!

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:55.208
How the hell did you get in here?

00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:57.167
You don't even have ID cards, do you?

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.375
We're here on a field trip, but we got lost!

00:04:59.375 --> 00:05:02.042
We followed some guy and wound up here!

00:05:02.042 --> 00:05:04.958
--But since we're here...
let us do the countdown!

00:05:04.958 --> 00:05:05.875
--Ritsu, any of these control-room computers would work, right?
--But since we're here... let us do the countdown!

00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:09.667
--Ritsu, any of these control-room computers would work, right?
--I don't care how cute you are--no! Authorized personnel only!

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.417
--Right.
--Aw, I wanna push the launch button!

00:05:11.417 --> 00:05:13.667
--Time to plug this in and scram.
--Aw, I wanna push the launch button!

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:15.875
--Time to plug this in and scram.
--Hey! Tickling won't help!

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:21.333
Security analysis complete!

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:26.208
I've placed a remote-control virus
on the control-room computer.

00:05:26.208 --> 00:05:31.458
Now the control center and
its system will act on my command.

00:05:31.458 --> 00:05:33.583
That's the first hurdle cleared.

00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:35.417
I know it's sudden, Ritsu,

00:05:35.417 --> 00:05:38.292
but a part of our entry route is aboveground.

00:05:38.292 --> 00:05:40.042
Can you do something?

00:05:40.042 --> 00:05:44.167
Roger. Checking your current position...

00:05:45.583 --> 00:05:46.833
Done!

00:05:46.833 --> 00:05:50.292
I'll turn off the corresponding
camera for ten seconds.

00:05:50.292 --> 00:05:51.375
Roger that.

00:05:51.375 --> 00:05:55.167
Three... two... one... zero!

00:06:09.417 --> 00:06:13.500
Security guard passing through.
Next patrol in ten minutes.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.500
Surveillance camera angle correction complete.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.542
It's not off, so please be careful.

00:06:19.542 --> 00:06:20.958
Got it.

00:06:30.625 --> 00:06:34.583
A fifty-meter staircase to the rocket hatch...

00:06:35.958 --> 00:06:37.875
Koro Sensei?!

00:06:39.042 --> 00:06:41.167
Inspection? Perfection!

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:43.542
Any accident would be a liability issue.

00:06:43.542 --> 00:06:45.750
Please don't say such awful things!

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.708
I'm relaying recorded footage
of the dummies to the control room.

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:53.333
If you swap them out now,
you won't get caught!

00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:55.833
C'mon, Karma.

00:06:57.792 --> 00:07:04.625
100, 99, 98, 97, 96, 95,

00:07:04.625 --> 00:07:08.125
94, 93, 92,

00:07:08.125 --> 00:07:11.042
91, 90, 89,

00:07:11.042 --> 00:07:15.708
--Liquid oxygen and liquid hydrogen systems are go.
--88, 87, 86...

00:07:15.708 --> 00:07:17.208
Are they going to be okay?

00:07:17.208 --> 00:07:18.750
--25, 24, 23,

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.583
--Flight mode on.
--25, 24, 23,

00:07:20.583 --> 00:07:25.250
22, 21, 20, 19...

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:30.125
You know, we've felt this
kind of nervous before, you and me.

00:07:30.125 --> 00:07:31.500
Yeah.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:37.125
But... we might've changed a little since then.

00:07:37.125 --> 00:07:40.000
--All systems go.
--5, 4, 3, 2, 1...

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.833
--Main engine ignition.
--5, 4, 3, 2, 1...

00:07:43.833 --> 00:07:47.708
--SRB ignition.
--1, 2, 3...

00:07:52.208 --> 00:07:53.958
Liftoff.

00:08:13.542 --> 00:08:15.125
It's fast, all right!

00:08:15.125 --> 00:08:17.500
Why did <i>you </i>tag along, Koro Sensei?!

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:20.542
Well, you know, I worry.

00:08:20.542 --> 00:08:23.833
Don't be overly concerned
about getting that data on me!

00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:28.625
You're on a journey through space--enjoy it!

00:08:31.958 --> 00:08:36.083
Koro Sensei...
there's something I'd like to say.

00:08:36.083 --> 00:08:41.625
You use every ounce of your life
to give us opportunities to learn.

00:08:41.625 --> 00:08:44.708
And we're really grateful for that.

00:08:44.708 --> 00:08:51.458
But your life means more to us
than just teaching material.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:56.125
I know. And I'm glad.

00:09:00.417 --> 00:09:03.292
S-So <i>fast</i>!

00:09:05.375 --> 00:09:10.542
You need to be traveling
at Mach 23 to enter space.

00:09:10.542 --> 00:09:17.000
Today, for the first time,
we were faster than Koro Sensei.

00:09:22.042 --> 00:09:26.042
"Assassination Classroom, Final Season"
"by Karma Akabane"

00:09:42.875 --> 00:09:47.125
Rendezvous complete. Commence HTV catch.

00:09:47.125 --> 00:09:48.583
Roger.

00:09:48.583 --> 00:09:52.083
Mechanical arm: operation verified.

00:09:52.083 --> 00:09:54.042
Three more meters.

00:09:54.042 --> 00:09:57.792
Two meters. One meter.

00:10:02.667 --> 00:10:07.792
HTV catch complete. Commence gripping.

00:10:11.917 --> 00:10:15.750
Demonstration ship: grip complete.

00:10:20.667 --> 00:10:22.917
Docking complete.

00:10:22.917 --> 00:10:25.917
Shield interface: all green.
Air pressure: normal.

00:10:25.917 --> 00:10:29.958
Permission granted to open hatch.
Welcome to the space station.

00:10:29.958 --> 00:10:32.375
Your country sent you a doll to play with.

00:10:32.375 --> 00:10:35.875
How about welcoming it aboard
and giving it a big hug?

00:10:35.875 --> 00:10:37.292
Okay!

00:10:43.292 --> 00:10:45.875
Huh? Where's the dummy?

00:10:45.875 --> 00:10:47.458
What?!

00:10:47.458 --> 00:10:50.333
Huh? A communications error?

00:10:50.333 --> 00:10:51.542
What's wrong?

00:10:51.542 --> 00:10:52.500
Huh?!

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.958
H-Hello...

00:10:53.958 --> 00:10:57.833
Hey, it's Mizui! I've seen <i>you </i>on TV!

00:10:57.833 --> 00:11:00.917
Wh-Why is there a kid in here
instead of a dummy?

00:11:00.917 --> 00:11:02.458
Hey, what's--

00:11:02.458 --> 00:11:04.875
I have terminated the comm-link with Earth!

00:11:04.875 --> 00:11:06.875
Thanks, Ritsu.

00:11:07.875 --> 00:11:11.708
We have a bomb.
We would like to do this peacefully.

00:11:11.708 --> 00:11:14.833
Please back away so we can talk.

00:11:14.833 --> 00:11:17.458
This place is a little cramped.

00:11:17.458 --> 00:11:20.167
Let's talk somewhere with more space.

00:11:20.167 --> 00:11:22.500
Come on--move it.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:31.917
Therefore, please allow us
to copy the American team's data.

00:11:31.917 --> 00:11:35.000
We won't be making any other demands.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.958
I think you know, but our teacher is a monster.

00:11:38.958 --> 00:11:44.792
I don't know what he'll do
to the earth if you refuse.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.875
Uh-oh--these guys calmed down way too quick.

00:11:50.875 --> 00:11:54.042
That's a career astronaut for you.

00:11:54.708 --> 00:11:59.625
First, let me give you two
daring kids a hand. Bravo.

00:11:59.625 --> 00:12:01.792
Oh--Japanese!

00:12:01.792 --> 00:12:06.083
But are you really gonna take on
the six of us--soldiers included?

00:12:06.083 --> 00:12:09.167
A bomb doesn't scare us.

00:12:09.167 --> 00:12:10.875
Because...

00:12:10.875 --> 00:12:13.667
...we've been running
experiments here, not knowing when

00:12:13.667 --> 00:12:16.542
this is all gonna blow up and kill us all.

00:12:20.917 --> 00:12:26.167
Enough pointless conflict.
This is no place to fight.

00:12:26.167 --> 00:12:29.000
We'll talk, so please, let him go.

00:12:33.958 --> 00:12:38.583
Even if you <i>do </i>steal the data,
how are you going to get home?

00:12:38.583 --> 00:12:41.375
Are you going to ask us
for help while you hijack us?

00:12:41.375 --> 00:12:43.167
We can make it back on our own.

00:12:43.167 --> 00:12:47.042
Our classmate's worked out
the return orbital calculations perfectly.

00:12:47.042 --> 00:12:48.208
Yep!

00:12:48.208 --> 00:12:52.208
Our teacher can do any fine-tuning
by pushing us in midair.

00:12:52.208 --> 00:12:54.000
This is way too reckless!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:59.625
Maybe you're just young,
but aren't you taking your lives too lightly?

00:12:59.625 --> 00:13:02.458
I didn't come here because I wanted to.

00:13:02.458 --> 00:13:06.833
I came because my friend asked me to.

00:13:06.833 --> 00:13:08.250
Karma...

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.667
And you mentioned our lives.

00:13:10.667 --> 00:13:13.917
We've done plenty
of thinking about that lately.

00:13:13.917 --> 00:13:18.625
I mean, we're students of
a class that'll kill its teacher.

00:13:18.625 --> 00:13:24.667
We should know by now
to be prepared to face life <i>with </i>life.

00:13:24.667 --> 00:13:27.542
Just like you--right?

00:13:27.542 --> 00:13:32.000
It seems you have genuine faith
in your target's plans...

00:13:33.958 --> 00:13:35.375
All right.

00:13:35.375 --> 00:13:38.833
I'll take it upon myself
to accept the hijackers' demands.

00:13:38.833 --> 00:13:39.792
Prepare the data.

00:13:39.792 --> 00:13:41.042
Huh?

00:13:41.042 --> 00:13:45.667
But first, help us offload supplies.

00:13:45.667 --> 00:13:49.458
We'll put you to work
and get you out of here already.

00:13:52.958 --> 00:13:57.292
I think they must have wanted
to give us junior-high kids

00:13:57.292 --> 00:13:59.958
the experience of a lifetime.

00:14:02.042 --> 00:14:04.333
This might just save him.

00:14:04.333 --> 00:14:06.083
Yeah...

00:14:06.083 --> 00:14:09.167
And that'd be enough for you, right?

00:14:09.167 --> 00:14:10.625
What do you mean?

00:14:10.625 --> 00:14:15.833
Well, I'm not going against
the class's decision to save him...

00:14:15.833 --> 00:14:21.917
...I'm just wondering what
Koro Sensei wants us to do.

00:14:24.833 --> 00:14:29.250
That's the lab data on preventing
that supercreature from exploding.

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:30.958
No signs of falsification.

00:14:30.958 --> 00:14:34.333
I can confirm it's the full data
from the experiment in question.

00:14:34.333 --> 00:14:36.458
I'll just grab a copy.

00:14:36.458 --> 00:14:38.375
It's copied.

00:14:38.375 --> 00:14:40.458
Now to get back and validate it.

00:14:40.458 --> 00:14:43.750
Yeah, we don't want to overstay our welcome.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.458
Hey, pops!

00:14:45.458 --> 00:14:47.083
You can keep this.

00:14:47.083 --> 00:14:48.917
Whoa, whoa! Hey!

00:14:48.917 --> 00:14:51.708
Honestly, there's just
some sweet bean jelly inside.

00:14:51.708 --> 00:14:54.500
Oh, no!

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.708
Just say you were too spooked
by the bomb to disobey.

00:14:57.708 --> 00:15:00.292
We're really sorry
for the trouble we've caused!

00:15:00.292 --> 00:15:03.000
At least it killed some time, right?

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:08.000
Swimming in zero gravity
like they're at a friend's house,

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.125
negotiating for top-secret intel

00:15:09.125 --> 00:15:11.875
like they're bargaining at a penny-candy shop,

00:15:11.875 --> 00:15:16.583
piercing the atmosphere like they're
heading home from school...

00:15:16.583 --> 00:15:19.500
There's some pretty amazing
junior-high kids out there!

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:22.292
You guys are an awesome group of heroes.

00:15:22.292 --> 00:15:25.292
Come back anytime--but next time,
do it the right way.

00:15:25.292 --> 00:15:27.792
I've had enough. However...

00:15:27.792 --> 00:15:31.833
...I'll make sure to increase
the budget for space exploration

00:15:31.833 --> 00:15:33.750
when I get in power.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:36.167
Yeah--I'm lookin' forward to it.

00:15:39.667 --> 00:15:42.250
Our time in space sure went by in a flash.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.417
Mmm-hmm.

00:15:43.417 --> 00:15:48.917
Now to see if we can get back
to Earth in one piece. Ritsu?

00:15:48.917 --> 00:15:50.958
Ritsu...?

00:15:50.958 --> 00:15:57.542
I'm on it. I've crunched a <i>ton</i>
of numbers to get you down safely.

00:15:57.542 --> 00:16:01.542
This spaceship may as well
be my own body by now.

00:16:01.542 --> 00:16:08.417
Plus, all those sensors I have
are picking up more than ever before.

00:16:08.417 --> 00:16:13.292
External temperature,
air pressure, speed, the scenery...

00:16:13.292 --> 00:16:15.042
Nagisa, Karma...

00:16:15.042 --> 00:16:18.500
I even have a clear read on
your respiration, your conversation,

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:21.208
your heartrate, your warmth.

00:16:21.208 --> 00:16:26.792
To think so much, to move, to feel...

00:16:26.792 --> 00:16:28.375
How wonderful...

00:16:28.375 --> 00:16:31.375
This mission has evolved my intelligence--

00:16:31.375 --> 00:16:33.625
I'm experiencing it firsthand!

00:16:34.333 --> 00:16:37.083
Hey, you two...

00:16:37.083 --> 00:16:41.583
I just gained awareness of
an emotion for the very first time.

00:16:41.583 --> 00:16:47.917
I'm happy. Happy to be a part of this class.

00:17:14.083 --> 00:17:19.250
Right on schedule! And what
a grueling trip it must have--ow!

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:21.125
Koro Sensei!

00:17:22.542 --> 00:17:26.000
So I didn't need to intercede
in the negotiations after all!

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:29.792
You really must have
gotten through to those spaceguys!

00:17:29.792 --> 00:17:30.958
Guess so.

00:17:30.958 --> 00:17:32.917
Now to give you boys a little shove.

00:17:32.917 --> 00:17:36.125
Hup! Ow! Hup! Hot! Ow! Hot!

00:17:36.125 --> 00:17:38.583
Onward to--ow!

00:17:44.583 --> 00:17:47.667
Hey, they made it! They're back!

00:17:47.667 --> 00:17:49.667
Keep going! Almost there!

00:17:49.667 --> 00:17:54.250
We doubted, fretted, came apart and clashed...

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:57.750
And finally, at the end of that long month...

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:59.833
...we went to space.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:04.750
Hooray! Yay! They did it!

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:05.625
Phew...

00:18:05.625 --> 00:18:08.292
--What in God's name have you done?
--Urk!

00:18:08.292 --> 00:18:11.458
I can't even <i>conceive </i>of how much
apologizing this will take!

00:18:11.458 --> 00:18:15.417
I-I threatened the students into going!

00:18:15.417 --> 00:18:18.583
You two aren't at all responsible--
you didn't know my plan.

00:18:18.583 --> 00:18:22.208
Besides, we got a nice bonus out of it!

00:18:22.208 --> 00:18:25.500
Data from using
real humans instead of dummies.

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:29.167
This alone should make another
rocket launch worthwhile.

00:18:29.167 --> 00:18:34.125
<i>And </i>Ritsu discovered
a more efficient course into space.

00:18:34.125 --> 00:18:38.000
Take all this and we'll call it even.

00:18:39.083 --> 00:18:41.208
You miscreant.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.375
We're home!

00:18:49.542 --> 00:19:02.292
<i>Once this season comes for me, I won't be able</i>

00:19:02.292 --> 00:19:07.542
<i>To search out your figure anymore</i>

00:19:07.542 --> 00:19:13.250
<i>I'll never forget</i>

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:19.875
<i>Until the day I can see you again</i>

00:19:32.083 --> 00:19:32.583
"Staff Room"

00:19:32.583 --> 00:19:35.292
"Staff Room"
Whoa! Check out this data!

00:19:35.292 --> 00:19:38.917
I'm glad you got it, but with
all this jargon--I can't understand a word!

00:19:38.917 --> 00:19:42.667
I'll handle it. Let's see here...

00:19:42.667 --> 00:19:47.042
"An experiment in space
proved that the risk of explosion

00:19:47.042 --> 00:19:50.458
for a tentacle creature
is inversely proportional to its size.

00:19:50.458 --> 00:19:52.167
The bigger it is, the more stable,

00:19:52.167 --> 00:19:55.542
while the smaller ones have
a higher likelihood of exploding.

00:19:55.542 --> 00:19:57.625
Unlike those the size of a small mouse,

00:19:57.625 --> 00:19:59.292
the probability of a human-sized creature

00:19:59.292 --> 00:20:04.667
going berserk and exploding
is much lower than expected."

00:20:04.667 --> 00:20:06.875
Huh? That means...

00:20:06.875 --> 00:20:10.250
"Additionally, the drug
indicated below is administered

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:14.500
and a silicon compound is periodically
stimulated to flow through the body.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:17.708
Simply put, by 'relieving muscular stiffness,'

00:20:17.708 --> 00:20:21.458
the risk of them going berserk
decreases dramatically."

00:20:21.458 --> 00:20:22.750
"Stiffness"?

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.875
"When the following conditions are satisfied...

00:20:24.875 --> 00:20:27.708
...the possibility of explosion,
even at the highest...

00:20:27.708 --> 00:20:29.375
...is less than one percent."

00:20:29.375 --> 00:20:31.875
One percent?!

00:20:31.875 --> 00:20:36.917
"It is likely that other cells
will die out before any explosion occurs,

00:20:36.917 --> 00:20:40.458
and the creature will gently
evaporate within 90 years."

00:20:40.458 --> 00:20:43.375
So can you make this drug or what?

00:20:43.375 --> 00:20:46.208
It's surprisingly easy! In fact...

00:20:46.208 --> 00:20:46.625
"Phew..."
It's surprisingly easy! In fact...

00:20:46.625 --> 00:20:48.125
"Phew..."
...I made one almost exactly like it before.

00:20:48.125 --> 00:20:49.958
...I made one almost exactly like it before.

00:20:49.958 --> 00:20:51.667
<i>That </i>one?!

00:20:52.417 --> 00:20:53.792
You're kidding me!

00:20:53.792 --> 00:20:57.000
The key to solving this
was right there all along?!

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.500
Are you sure? I mean,
it was almost too easy to find.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:04.542
No--the road here wasn't all that easy.

00:21:04.542 --> 00:21:06.125
Kayano...

00:21:06.125 --> 00:21:08.833
Because my sister
risked her life to stop Koro Sensei

00:21:08.833 --> 00:21:11.792
as he was turning into a destructive creature.

00:21:11.792 --> 00:21:14.458
Because Koro Sensei followed in her footsteps,

00:21:14.458 --> 00:21:18.625
risking his life to teach us.

00:21:18.625 --> 00:21:21.000
If we hadn't risked our lives,

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:24.000
we probably wouldn't
be able to make that drug,

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:26.750
and we wouldn't have grown into
a class that could look for answers

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:28.500
way out in <i>space</i>.

00:21:29.375 --> 00:21:33.042
Either way, less than one percent
is as good as zero!

00:21:33.042 --> 00:21:37.167
Even if we can't kill him, Earth won't explode!

00:21:40.292 --> 00:21:42.708
Wait... what about the assassination?

00:21:42.708 --> 00:21:44.333
Huh?

00:21:44.333 --> 00:21:47.417
The one we've been
working on since our first term?

00:21:47.417 --> 00:21:50.125
Should we just call it off as of today?

00:21:50.125 --> 00:21:55.625
Huh? I... I guess we can. Wait...

00:21:58.667 --> 00:22:01.250
Nagisa! Whaddya wanna do?

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:03.458
This was <i>your </i>idea.

00:22:03.458 --> 00:22:06.250
No matter how minute the possibility,

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:08.667
the government won't cancel
its assassination plans,

00:22:08.667 --> 00:22:11.917
not as long as he remains a dangerous creature.

00:22:24.042 --> 00:22:26.292
I want to treat everyone's feelings with care,

00:22:26.292 --> 00:22:29.667
especially now that
we've come through that tunnel.

00:22:29.667 --> 00:22:32.458
Here's what we decided:

00:22:32.458 --> 00:22:35.250
If we couldn't kill Koro Sensei
by the March deadline,

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:37.417
we'd graduate from assassination

00:22:37.417 --> 00:22:40.292
and go back to being
plain old students and teacher.

00:22:40.292 --> 00:22:44.792
But until that deadline,
we'd wield our blades with conviction.

00:22:44.792 --> 00:22:50.042
After all, here "assassination"
is our bond with our teacher--

00:22:50.042 --> 00:22:54.750
and a compulsory course
from Koro Sensei, who'd nurtured us.

00:22:55.208 --> 00:22:59.734
That's what we made up our minds to do.
